msgid "Database and Weather Chaos"
msgstr ""

msgid "Beyond application-level chaos, the test suite also covers infrastructure-level failures using https://github.com/Shopify/toxiproxy[*Toxiproxy*] -- a TCP proxy that can inject latency, cut connections, and throttle bandwidth at the network layer:"
msgstr ""

msgid "*Database chaos* routes JDBC connections through Toxiproxy to MySQL:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Tests include slow queries (3s latency injection), connection pool exhaustion (4s latency + small pool + concurrent requests), and full database outages (connection cut). JDBC telemetry creates separate database query spans, so the AI sees `GET /poke (3019ms) -> SELECT ... (3015ms)` and can identify database-level root causes."
msgstr ""

msgid "*Weather API chaos* routes REST client calls through Toxiproxy to an external API:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Tests include slow external API responses and full API outages."
msgstr ""

msgid "No application code changes are required -- chaos is injected purely at the network layer via the Toxiproxy REST API."
msgstr ""

msgid "The Evaluation Mechanism: LLM-as-Judge"
msgstr ""

msgid "Each integration test follows the same pattern:"
msgstr ""

msgid "*Inject chaos* into the test application (or do nothing for baseline tests)"
msgstr ""

msgid "*Wait* for telemetry to propagate to LGTM"
msgstr ""

msgid "*Run analysis* via `GET /analyze/\\{n}`"
msgstr ""

msgid "*Capture* all tool outputs (raw telemetry data the LLM saw)"
msgstr ""

msgid "*Score* the analysis using a separate LLM call"
msgstr ""

msgid "The scoring uses an `AnalysisEvaluationStrategy` that builds a detailed evaluation prompt containing:"
msgstr ""

msgid "The original telemetry data (traces, logs, metrics) the AI analyzed"
msgstr ""

msgid "The system prompt used for analysis"
msgstr ""

msgid "The analysis output being evaluated"
msgstr ""

msgid "Scenario-specific evaluation criteria"
msgstr ""

msgid "A judge LLM (`EvaluationJudge`) then scores the analysis on four dimensions, each worth 0-25 points:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Dimension"
msgstr ""

msgid "What It Measures"
msgstr ""

msgid "*Completeness*"
msgstr ""

msgid "Did it find all the issues present in the telemetry?"
msgstr ""

msgid "*Accuracy*"
msgstr ""

msgid "Are the identified root causes correct?"
msgstr ""

msgid "*Correlation Quality*"
msgstr ""

msgid "Did it properly link traces, logs, and metrics?"
msgstr ""

msgid "*Actionability*"
msgstr ""

msgid "Are the remediation suggestions useful and specific?"
msgstr ""

msgid "The passing threshold defaults to *70/100*. Set `EVALUATION_THRESHOLD` to override it for any test script:"
msgstr ""

msgid "If the score falls below the threshold, the evaluation also outputs *prompt improvement suggestions* -- concrete changes to the system prompt that would improve analysis quality. This creates a feedback loop: run tests, get scores, improve the prompt, run tests again."
msgstr ""

msgid "Cross-LLM Combinations"
msgstr ""

msgid "A critical design choice is that the *analyzer LLM* and the *scorer LLM* can be different providers. This prevents self-evaluation bias -- an LLM scoring its own output might be systematically lenient."
msgstr ""

